3 V-b. The department shall not issue an approval for a new landfill or a landfill expansion
4 unless the application includes as part of the facility’s proposed operating plan leachate
5 management procedures that provide for safe and effective management of leachate throughout the
6 lifeofthefacility,includingthepost-closureperiod. Theleachatemanagementplanshallinclude,at
7 minimum, a description of how leachate will be collected and stored on-site, if and how it will be
8 treated on-site, how it will be transported off-site, the type of leachate disposal facility the applicant
9 proposes to use, a statement of the projected frequency of leachate transports per week, and
10 contingency plans for leachate disposal capacity constraints. Before issuing an operating approval
11 for a new landfill or a landfill expansion, the permittee shall provide the department with
12 documentation of contractual arrangements between the permittee and at least 2 leachate disposal
13 facilities demonstrating that the permittee will be able to comply with the leachate disposal
14 provisions of its operating plan. The permittee shall promptly (1) notify the department if its
15 contractual arrangements with a leachate disposal facility are modified in a way that affects the
16 permittee’s ability to comply with its operating plan and (2) provide the department with
17 documentationofanycontractualarrangementwithanysubstituteleachatedisposalfacilityentered
18 into after the landfill or landfill expansion becomes operational such that the department has
19 documentation of at least 2 current arrangements throughout the life of the facility, including the
20 post-closureperiod.
